<%# THE FRAME THE PANEL ON THE PLAY PAGE FETCHES INTO, and the whole of this
    response when Turbo asked for it.

    The id is the one `turns/_turn` draws, so Turbo matches the frame it asked
    for; with scripts blocked this same action renders under the game's layout
    instead (see `MachineryController`) and the frame element is an ordinary
    wrapper the browser draws right through. %>
<turbo-frame id="<%= dom_id(@scene, :machinery) %>">
  <%= render "machinery/panel", machinery: @machinery %>
</turbo-frame>
